{{also|Lint}}
==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|lynet}}, {{m|enm|linet}}, from {{der|en|fro|linette||grain of flax}}, diminutive of {{m|fro|lin||flax}}; or, from {{etyl|Medieval Latin|en}} {{m|la|linteum}}, from {{der|en|la|līnum||flax}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/lɪnt/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-lint.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪnt}}
* {{homophones|en|Lent|q1=with [[pin-pen merger]]}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# A [[fine]] [[material]] made by [[scraping]] [[cotton]] or [[linen]] [[cloth]]; used for [[dressing]] [[wound]]s.
# [[clinging|Clinging]] [[fuzzy]] [[fluff]] that clings to fabric or [[accumulate]]s in one's [[pocket]]s or [[navel]] etc.
#: {{ux|en|clean the '''lint''' out of the vacuum cleaner's filter.}}
# The [[fibrous]] [[coat]] of thick [[hair]]s covering the [[seed]]s of the [[cotton]] [[plant]].
# [[raw|Raw]] [[cotton]] ready for [[bale|baling]].

